Next, calculate the total amount of water each group drinks. Add the water the linemen drink to the water the skill position players drink:

96 + 60 = 156 ounces

The cooler can hold 126 ounces of water.  The water the linemen drank is 96 ounces and that is the same as 96/126 of the total.    Therefore, the part of the water in the cooler that is left after the linemen drank their water is 126 - 96 = 30 ounces.   So, the water the skill position players drank is 30% of the water in the cooler.

The operation is 80/30 x 100 = 266. If the students drank 268 ounces and the cooler water is 126 ounces, then, in the next round, the skill position players were a ordered.  They don't talk to one another at all.

Now multiply those 266 by 100. <|end_of_text|>
