To find the time it takes for the water to fill the basin, divide the total volume of water by the rate of flow: 

Time = (Total volume of water)/(Rate of flow per second)

Time = (260 gallons)/(20 gallons per second)

Time = 13 seconds

So the basin will fill in 13 seconds, and we can write it as \boxed{13} seconds.<|end_of_text|>
